# Renderer authoring

A renderer is a presentation-only WebAssembly Component. It imports nothing and exports one typed function from `upwell:renderer/renderer@0.1.0`. Generate guest bindings from the exact committed WIT; never hand-declare canonical ABI core-Wasm symbols. Register command formats and compatibility requirements in <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/extensions">catalog extensions</GuideRef>; this page owns the executable guest.

## Use the canonical contract

The canonical file is <SrcRef path="crates/cargo-upwell/wit/renderer.wit"><code>crates/cargo-upwell/wit/renderer.wit</code></SrcRef>. Its complete contract is:

```text
package upwell:renderer@0.1.0;

/// Capability-free presentation contract implemented by user renderer components.
///
/// Components must import nothing from the host and export the typed `render`
/// function below. Guest projects should generate bindings from this WIT world
/// instead of naming canonical-ABI core Wasm symbols directly.
world renderer {
    /// Bounded canonical command projection selected and validated by the host.
    record render-request {
        abi-version: string,
        command: string,
        format: string,
        media-type: string,
        tooling-schema: string,
        resources: list<string>,
        color: bool,
        payload: list<u8>,
    }

    /// Presentation bytes plus claims the host verifies against the request.
    record render-response {
        format: string,
        media-type: string,
        resources: list<string>,
        body: list<u8>,
    }

    /// Required component-level export. An error triggers the native fallback.
    export render: func(request: render-request) -> result<render-response, string>;
}
```

Copy or reference that file in the guest project and use the language's Component Model binding generator. A partial duplicate will drift when fields or package versions change.

## Implement the minimal guest

The framework repository does not contain a renderer guest fixture, so this workflow pins the standard Rust Component Model toolchain used to validate the example: Rust `1.97.1`, `wit-bindgen` `0.57.1`, `wasm-tools` `1.247.0`, and `wasm32-unknown-unknown`. The guest is `no_std` so the result has no WASI imports.

Create this manifest:

```toml
[package]
name = "summary-renderer"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"

[lib]
crate-type = ["cdylib"]

[dependencies]
wit-bindgen = { version = "=0.57.1", default-features = false, features = ["macros", "realloc"] }
wee_alloc = "=0.4.5"

[profile.release]
lto = true
opt-level = "s"
panic = "abort"
strip = "symbols"
```

Place the exact contract above at `wit/renderer.wit`, then implement `src/lib.rs` with the generated root-world `Guest` trait and generated `export!` macro:

```rust
#![no_std]

extern crate alloc;

#[global_allocator]
static ALLOCATOR: wee_alloc::WeeAlloc = wee_alloc::WeeAlloc::INIT;

mod bindings {
    wit_bindgen::generate!({
        path: "wit/renderer.wit",
        world: "renderer",
    });

    use super::SummaryRenderer;
    export!(SummaryRenderer);
}

use alloc::format;
use alloc::string::String;
use bindings::{Guest, RenderRequest, RenderResponse};

#[panic_handler]
fn panic(_: &core::panic::PanicInfo<'_>) -> ! {
    core::arch::wasm32::unreachable()
}

struct SummaryRenderer;

impl Guest for SummaryRenderer {
    fn render(request: RenderRequest) -> Result<RenderResponse, String> {
        if request.command != "inspect" {
            return Err(format!("unsupported command: {}", request.command));
        }

        let payload = String::from_utf8(request.payload)
            .map_err(|error| format!("inspect payload is not UTF-8: {error}"))?;
        let body = format!(
            "resources: {}\ncanonical-bytes: {}\n",
            request.resources.len(),
            payload.len(),
        )
        .into_bytes();

        Ok(RenderResponse {
            format: request.format,
            media_type: request.media_type,
            resources: request.resources,
            body,
        })
    }
}
```

The guest accepts only `inspect`, treats the command projection as canonical UTF-8 bytes, and echoes the host-selected format, media type, and resource set. A real renderer may decode the command's canonical JSON payload, but it must not fabricate resource identities outside `request.resources`.

## Build a component

Build and inspect the component with the pinned commands:

```sh
rustup toolchain install 1.97.1 --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo install --locked wasm-tools --version 1.247.0

cargo +1.97.1 generate-lockfile
cargo +1.97.1 build --locked --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown

wasm-tools component new \
  target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/summary_renderer.wasm \
  -o components/summary.component.wasm

wasm-tools component wit components/summary.component.wasm
```

`wit-bindgen` emits the component type and canonical ABI around `render`; `wasm-tools component new` packages that core Wasm into the component artifact the catalog registers. Inspect the packaged component, not the core module. The inspection output must have no `import` lines and must include:

```text
package upwell:renderer@0.1.0 {
  world renderer {
    export render: func(request: render-request) -> result<render-response, string>;
  }
}
```

Commit `Cargo.lock`, the copied WIT file, the source, and `components/summary.component.wasm`. Record a digest for the packaged catalog artifact.

## Register the artifact

```toml
schema = "1"

[[entries]]
type = "renderer"
id = "acme/summary"
component = "components/summary.component.wasm"
commands = ["inspect"]
format = "summary"
media-type = "text/plain"
extension = "txt"
output-file = true
abi = "^0.1"
tooling-schema = "^0.20"
utf8 = true
```

The host validates the ABI requirement against 0.1.0, the document tooling schema, catalog claims, and component contract before invocation.

Verify catalog selection and host invocation with the format declared above:

```sh
cargo upwell inspect \
  --catalog .upwell/catalog.toml \
  --format summary
```

If compilation, instantiation, execution, UTF-8 validation, or response-claim validation fails, Cargo Upwell reports the renderer failure and uses the command's native fallback rather than treating renderer output as canonical application data.

## Respect sandbox and response claims

<Symbol path="cargo_upwell::renderer::component::ComponentRendererHost" /> rejects any host import. It bounds component/input/output bytes, resource count, metadata length, fuel, wall-clock execution, guest memory, tables, and instances. Compilation runs in a separate bounded/deadlined worker.

The response must preserve the requested format and media type. Every response resource must have been selected by the host. `utf8 = true` requires a valid UTF-8 body.

<Callout type="warning" title="Presentation only">

A renderer must not discover application facts, modify the tooling document, or perform policy checks hidden from canonical diagnostics. It renders host-selected canonical input. Return `Err` for unsupported input and let the native fallback preserve command usability.

</Callout>

## Troubleshoot authoring

- `InvalidComponent`: verify Component Model output and the exact exported world.
- `HostImport`: remove WASI/filesystem/network/clock/random imports and runtime initialization that requests them.
- ABI or tooling-schema mismatch: align catalog requirements with the committed WIT/tooling contract.
- Response claim failure: echo format/media type exactly and return only selected resources.
- Invalid UTF-8: emit text or declare `utf8 = false` with an appropriate binary media type.

Continue with <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers/testing-and-failures">renderer testing and failures</GuideRef> and <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/extensions">catalog extensions</GuideRef>.
